  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "A bag contains 5 red balls and 3 blue balls, for a total of 8 balls. If 2 balls are drawn at random, what is the probability of drawing 2 red balls?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "5/14",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Interpret the draw as uniform sampling without replacement from the eight distinct balls. Number the balls \\(1,\\ldots,8\\), with the red balls numbered \\(1,\\ldots,5\\). List each pair with its smaller number first, so every possible pair is counted exactly once. There are \\(7+6+\\cdots+1=28\\) equally likely pairs in total and \\(4+3+2+1=10\\) pairs of red balls. Therefore the probability of drawing two red balls is\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{28}=\\frac{5}{14}.\n\\]",
